      {
        "id": "pthm-td-concave-stability",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Concave entropy, constrained maxima, and local stability",
        "statement": "Let $C$ be an open convex region of dimensionless numerical coordinates for a compound of independent separated systems, and let $S_{\\mathrm{tot}}:C\\to\\mathbb R$ be the adopted $C^2$ concave total entropy on a smooth single-phase chart. Let the feasible set be the affine slice $F=C\\cap\\{x:Ax=b\\}$ for a fixed real linear map $A$ and vector $b$. For the following conclusions, assume the mathematical input that for differentiable concave $f$ on an open convex $C$, an interior point of $C\\cap\\{x:Ax=b\\}$ whose derivative vanishes on $\\ker A$ is a global feasible maximizer; strict concavity gives at most one maximizer; for $C^2$ concave $f$, the Hessian quadratic form is negative semidefinite. Under this input, if $x_*\\in F$ is interior relative to this slice and $DS_{\\mathrm{tot}}(x_*)$ vanishes on $\\ker A$, then $x_*$ is a global entropy maximum on $F$. If $S_{\\mathrm{tot}}$ is strictly concave on $F$, that maximum is unique. The Hessian conclusion does not by itself give strict stability.\n\nThe mathematical input is supplied by [[lem-tdmath-concave-affine-maximizer-and-hessian]] on the stated region and admissible affine segments.\n\nThere is a further conditional scaling conclusion. On a designated open single-phase bulk cone $C_c\\subseteq D_c$ with the common constitutive law adopted by [[post-td-common-bulk-constitutive-law]], the $C^2$ entropy Hessian has zero radial direction: $D^2S_c(x)[h,x]=0$ for every $x\\in C_c$ and every vector $h$. This branch adopts coordinate-preserving entropy transport between the distinct scaled-system tag and one fixed material-law chart, with common species, units and reference conventions. The null-direction conclusion is not asserted for the general tagged family from [[post-td-concave-fundamental-entropy]] and [[post-td-bulk-additivity]] alone.",
        "deps": [
          "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain",
          "def-td-isolated-compound-feasible-set",
          "post-td-bulk-additivity",
          "post-td-concave-fundamental-entropy",
          "post-td-common-bulk-constitutive-law",
          "lem-tdmath-concave-affine-maximizer-and-hessian",
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-isolated-compound-feasible-set": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "post-td-bulk-additivity": "physical-assumption",
          "post-td-concave-fundamental-entropy": "physical-assumption",
          "post-td-common-bulk-constitutive-law": "physical-assumption",
          "lem-tdmath-concave-affine-maximizer-and-hessian": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "provenance": {
